2026-10-15T17:32:19.0871092Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-15T17:32:19.0880938Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-15T17:32:19.0881407Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-15T17:32:19.0881701Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-15T17:32:19.0881847Z 
2026-10-15T17:32:19.0881962Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-15T17:32:19.0882155Z 
2026-10-15T17:32:19.0882300Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-15T17:32:19.0882589Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-15T17:32:19.0882741Z 
2026-10-15T17:32:19.0882821Z If you would like to
2026-10-15T17:32:19.0883015Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-15T17:32:19.0883150Z 
2026-10-15T17:32:19.0883281Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-15T17:32:19.0883533Z   $ sh ./install-nix
